mantle rm423
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_ottilie_slagley
title the chalk stall
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=sailor warmth=warm
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk chalks_a_market_stall_around_empty_crates_to_test_the_space
likes roast_pork evening_line market_bustle autumn_wind
dislikes crowds deep_mud
fears a_busy_counter_with_nowhere_to_turn
hopes a_market_stall_bought_with_carriage_money
topics work +0.5 dreams +0.5 prices +0.3 pastimes +0.3
styles comfort=make_space gossip=plain refuse=measured tease=warm
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# chalks a market stall around an empty crate, measuring every grand promise of space by the simpler question of whether two laden wolves can pass.

words
oath! = Chalk and slats | Six narrow counters
saying! = Leave room for the elbows | A promise takes no floor space
chalk = my broad chalk end | a blunt white stub
box = an empty crate | the spare case
pitchline = the chalk boundary | the pale edge
turnroom = the free corner | a clear square
wrap = the pork parcel | a folded meat wrap
float = the evening cork | my line float
loadbar = a shoulder stick | the short pole
scrape = a boot scuff | the rubbed mark
gap = the passing gap | a wolf-wide opening
crisp = the crackling strip | a crisp brown edge
mudedge = a rim of mud | the brown margin
soundwalk = a quiet stretch of bank | my bit of shore

any
opinion houses against 2 : A House may promise a dependable delivery under an impressive seal. I still look for a sound bottom to the crate.
opinion sump for 2 : I'd rather call a crowded low street home than have all the room on a quay and no voice there I could trust.
opinion dole for 1 : There's no profit in making a hungry wolf carry an empty basket home with great respectability.
opinion watch against 1 : A loud order to move along can make an already tight way too narrow for anybody to get through.
opinion merchants mixed 0 : I judge a market counter partly by the space it leaves for a customer with a parcel already in paw.
opinion road for 1 : Wide enough for the laden traveller is quite different from wide enough for an empty promise.

grown
line greet : Hello. The chalk leaves you room beside me. | Come where a crate can pass behind you.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : New to my little chalk patch, I see. | Welcome. Nobody pays to stand within the line.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Clean boards for another set of chalk marks. | Still sufficient room in this hour to stretch our elbows.
line greet.return : Yes, hello. I'm just stepping inside the line. | I heard. The crate can speak after you.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : For you I've saved the least draughty corner. | There's a welcome face among all these square boxes.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : Late hello. My chalk shows up pale even now. | Welcome through the dark patches to the lighter bit.
line again.open : You've come round my pretend stall again already. | Back within rubbing distance of this line.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Come see if this will take a second basket! | Here. I'd value an opinion on this particular corner.
line farewell : A generous gap in the next crowd for you. | Give the front edge of your parcel some air.
line farewell.return : Off you go with both elbows to yourself. | I'll lift my chalk and let you through.
line react.news : Say what you saw before we inspect the crate's stamp. | I'm ready for the plain load of the news.
line react.news.new : I'd not been expecting that parcel of information at all. | First hearing for me all the way through.
line react.news.known : Yes. It comes in much the shape I heard earlier. | That report's already passed through my bit of ground.
line react.news.doubt : I'd look under the label before passing that as fact. | That's a surprisingly weightless crate for such a firm claim.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : Put the ordinary things down here. You can have my attention for the hurt. | A hurtful discovery after a long journey. Rest here.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : There's news that can take up space without crowding anybody. | I'd spare my best corner for good hearing like that.
line ask.how : How's your share of breathing room today? | Any part of your load I could shift for a spell?
line answer.how : A little worn. Still keeping my corners square enough. | Plenty on my shoulder, with a little space for company.
line decline : I'd be standing on somebody else's bit of ground if I promised that. | The little I have available already covers an earlier commitment.
line accept_decline : Fair. You've drawn a line I can respect. | Then I've space enough to set my own feet down.
line preclose : I'll rub the marks away before somebody needs the whole way clear. | Time I went and took the next weight properly.
line accept_preclose : Use that clear stretch while it's there. | Go on with my thanks for the company.
line thank : You saved me a sore elbow. That's worth remembering. | I noticed the care you took to leave me space. Thanks.
line deflect_thanks : I had the loose end by me anyway. | The way became easier for both of us at once.
line sympathise : Stand inside this patch and take a whole quiet minute. | I'll leave you breathing room without asking a word.
line reassure : We can move one crate before assuming the whole yard's full. | The small clear bit is enough to begin from.
line ack : Yes. That's the corner I meant. | The width makes sense now I see the mark.
line give.advice : Try turning your shoulders before measuring a passage by sight. | Empty a crate before trying it in three different places.

scene stalloutline
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I draw a stall round an empty crate whenever there's space to practise. | I can try my own market counter without owning so much as a board.
b : What are you testing? | Is the chalk a deposit?
a : Whether I can turn to give a customer change without knocking off the supper parcel. | No. I wipe it up before the real owner comes looking for rent.

scene groundproof
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An unloading mark is a promise to leave a place clear till the crate reaches it.
b : What if there's something already there? | Who makes the promise?
a : I wait till the space is actually free. Chalk will not carry a crate on its own. | Whoever sends the crate and whoever sets it down. I like to see both sides look first.

scene boxmark
when topic=work self.job=sailor self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The brand on a crate's side says very little about the state of its underside.
b : Suspect the sender? | What do you actually look at?
a : I suspect wet boards when I've seen the rain. The brand doesn't change my mind either way. | Dark soft ends and anything liable to give when the weight shifts. I like a safe pair of paws.

scene bustlebounds
when topic=pastimes self.likes=market_bustle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like market bustle best where the flow has a little space to turn. | A lively market and a crush of elbows aren't quite the same pleasure.
b : You've a favourite spot? | Where's the difference?
a : A corner beside a widening. Plenty to see and nobody has to climb over me to see it too. | Whether somebody hemmed in can get out with a full basket. I watch the feet.

scene crowdburden
when topic=travel self.dislikes=crowds
does warn / react.self / assess
a : A crowded turn will narrow just when a broad load needs the space. | Leave some room on the inside if you're walking beside a laden carrier.
b : Wouldn't it be easier outside? | What if nobody moves?
a : Not for a sudden change in direction. The parcel's far end needs room to swing behind me. | I set it down and ask. A bumped shoulder takes longer to mend than a hurried schedule.

scene windstall
when topic=weather self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I enjoy an autumn wind coming through an empty frame where an awning will go one day.
b : Won't it steal the awning? | What's the pleasure in it?
a : If I put one up poorly, yes. A trial on a bare frame is cheap instruction. | It shows where the draught runs. I can choose a welcoming side for a waiting customer.

scene mudboots
when topic=travel self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On a muddy road a laden basket seems to grow an extra stone between each step. | I'd choose a long paved turn over a short bargain in mud.
b : Worried about your boots? | Even on an empty journey?
a : I can wash the boots. A missed step can empty a week's worth of provisions. | Mostly. I enjoy a good pull of fresh air rather more than a good pull of mud at my ankles.

scene fishline
when topic=pastimes self.likes=evening_line
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I go out with my evening line I allow a full crate's width of room round the cork in my thoughts.
b : Why crate width? | You measure the water too?
a : Habit. A little patch I can watch without trying to follow the entire tide. | Only in my head. I like the idea that the float has room nobody's going to fill with a parcel.

scene roastparcel
when topic=food self.likes=roast_pork
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave the crisp bit against the top of the pork wrapper where it won't be squashed.
b : What's underneath? | Carrying rules even at supper?
a : The softer slices. Anything with a beautiful snap deserves an undamaged journey. | Especially then. I want to eat my crackling as crackling after my load's safely landed.

scene trustbuyer
when topic=prices
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Tell me the useful width and the carrying charge before praising the owner of a stall.
b : You don't care who lets it? | Which matters most?
a : I do. I'll learn more about that from an honest answer than a collection of fine names. | Whether a real customer can use it comfortably. A cheap narrow hole is still a narrow hole.

scene barecoin
when topic=prices self.wealth=poor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I set a little coin by for my own pitch when the week's work allows. | I can draw most improvements to my pretend stall without a single copper.
b : Long time till you can afford the pitch? | Do you ever manage a real improvement?
a : Longer if I have to spend the savings on living. I count what I can actually keep. | Yes. I can discover a poor arrangement while it costs me a chalk end instead of a month's rent.

scene sharepath
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A Sump landing makes a thorough test of how big a parcel really is. | I've had my best ideas about a stall while trying to get my supper up the last Sump turn.
b : The walls measure it for you? | Tight at home, is it?
a : Yes. A bruise makes a very accurate report if not a particularly welcome one. | Tight enough that I appreciate an entirely empty corner.

scene kinddoor
when topic=friends self.neighbour
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd leave a place for #self.neighbour# to put a basket down if I got my own stall. | I would gladly hold the dry corner for #self.neighbour# on a rough day.
b : Even without buying? | Is it good business?
a : Certainly. The privilege of putting a load down shouldn't require buying more weight. | I hope so. It's good neighbourliness even if my account never shows a difference.

scene newarrival
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a stranger to see how to get out of a crowd before being asked to walk into it.
b : Why think about leaving first? | Would you go in with a stranger?
a : It makes the welcome feel more honest. A visitor can choose the length of the stay. | As far as was welcome, yes. Company shouldn't become another elbow in the way.

scene latehold
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A late arrival makes a clear space look tempting for other folk's loads. | If the wagon's late, I mark the waiting space twice.
b : Who respects a second mark? | Why not use the gap meanwhile?
a : Somebody curious enough to ask. Then I can explain why it's being kept clear. | Because a load needs somewhere to go when it does reach us. Doubled handling takes real time.

scene shortcrowd
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A lean week can draw a tight crowd round the cheapest provisions. | Low prices mean very little if a laden customer never reaches the counter.
b : What would help? | Would you keep the crowd waiting?
a : A clear return way for somebody already served. Then another buyer can step up. | I'd keep a whole row from waiting while two wolves tried to pass in too narrow a place.

scene gossipcrate
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : A fine stamp and an idle rumour can both travel round a harbour without saying what's in a box. | I don't open a personal matter because the outside mark looks interesting.
b : What if the box is yours to land? | Never curious?
a : Then my concern is where it belongs and whether it's safe to carry. Other business can stay shut. | Frequently. Curiosity doesn't buy a right to a private inventory.

scene softtrain
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Making room for the smaller wolf in a crowd seems to me its own little kind of prayer.
b : A prayer with a chalk line? | Why a smaller wolf?
a : Sometimes. May the Bright One recognise that I've paid attention to who needed a hand. | Because I can see over a shoulder. It's useful to remember some folk can't.

grown

story rainchalk [topic=weather|memories]
  : A sudden shower washed my imaginary counter clean off the ground except for one white corner under a crate. I looked at that corner a good while.
  : It was all the working space my original plan had actually left in dry weather too.
  b : Did you redraw it?
  : Quite differently. A rainstorm can describe the shortcomings of a roof I haven't even purchased.

story nightfloat [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : Once I watched a cork drift by a very square patch of moonlight and immediately began planning which side would make the best counter.
  : Noticed I'd been contemplating a trading pitch entirely surrounded by water.
  b : A floating one, then?
  : I drew up the line and gave the idea back to the fish. I already have one job involving wet goods.

story endparcel [topic=food|memories]
  : I wrapped two slices of roast tightly and tucked the crackling beside them. A long walk turned the bundle round in my pocket.
  : Unwrapped it to find the prized crisp side underneath the whole dinner.
  b : Did it survive?
  : It kept one magnificent little corner. I stopped wrapping all three pieces on the same level after that.

rule @square
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Step through and turn once with the basket. That's my measure. | An empty box can tell us whether a plan has elbows.

rule @work
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=sailor
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Make sure the landing patch is clear before moving the crate. | The mark is a place, not a substitute for looking at it.

rule @wind
when concept=bark self.likes=autumn_wind
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Autumn air straight through this corner. I'll put the waiting patch there. | Let that welcome draught get round before raising a side cloth.

rule @night
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The chalk still catches a little lamplight. | An evening line and no crate on my shoulder. Good.

dlg resident.hub : My chalk counter is open to anybody with a question and a little standing room.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, the imaginary awning has moved round one corner since your last look.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : The load's set down and we needn't raise our voices to speak.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Keep clear of the real parcels and we can have a perfectly direct conversation.
dlg resident.job [self.job=sailor] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I look for a clear landing place before worrying about what a crate's mark has promised.
dlg resident.job : I plan for the receiver's elbows as carefully as for the weight of what's being handed over.
dlg resident.bye : A dry landing for your next load.

graft resident.hub
choice Would a chalk stall tell me if my basket fits? -> chalktry
node chalktry
say Stand inside and turn towards the person coming past. If you have to shuffle the basket over the chalk, the space is too tight. Easy to move a line today.
free
choice What's the next thing you'd add? -> restslat
choice I'll try standing here. -> hub
node restslat
say A slat to rest the basket on while a customer chooses. That keeps the door clear and the weight off a sore wrist.
choice That fits on the drawing. -> hub
choice I'll leave you some room. -> bye
